This is a technical constraint, not a policy preference: the Linux kernel BPF
verifier restricts most BPF helper functions, including those these probes
require, to programs that declare a GPL-compatible license. The exception
covers only the programs that run inside the kernel. The userspace loader, the
event normalizer and every other component of the agent are Apache-2.0.

Each source file under crates/sensors/linux/ebpf/ carries an
SPDX-License-Identifier line, which is authoritative for that file.
